---
// Comparison page. Copy authored against briefs/maltese-vs-maltipoo.json (2026-07-13).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import CaptionedBlock from '../components/CaptionedBlock.astro';
import FactsCard from '../components/FactsCard.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { site, whatsappLink } from '../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import featuredImg from '../assets/site/20-small-breeds-lineup.webp';

const title = 'Maltese vs Maltipoo: What the Poodle Changes | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  'Maltese vs Maltipoo for Singapore homes: what the Poodle cross changes in coat, trainability and care. Both HDB-listed; the honest differences from a shop placing both.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Compare Breeds', url: '/compare-maltipoo' },
  { name: 'Maltese vs Maltipoo', url: '/maltese-vs-maltipoo' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'Do Maltese shed more than Maltipoos?',
    a: 'Both are low-shedding by small-dog standards. The Maltese drops fine silky strands you will find on dark clothes; the Maltipoo’s curl traps loose hair in the coat instead, which means less on the sofa but more brushing to prevent mats. Pick your chore.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which is easier to train?',
    a: 'The Maltipoo, and it is noticeable. The Toy Poodle side speeds up toilet training and cue learning, which matters most for first-time owners. A Maltese trains fine too, just with more patience.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a price difference?',
    a: 'Our Maltipoos run $3,288 to $5,988 all-in. Maltese are placed by our parent brand Curious Tails, and pricing differs by litter; WhatsApp us and we will quote both honestly.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which lives longer?',
    a: 'Both sit in the long-lived small-dog class, commonly cited around 12 to 15 years. Care, weight and dental habits matter more than the breed choice here.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which is better for allergy-sensitive homes?',
    a: 'The Maltipoo’s curlier coat has the slight edge, but no dog is truly hypoallergenic. Meet the actual puppy in person before deciding; reactions are individual.',
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/maltese-vs-maltipoo',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'Maltese vs Maltipoo comparison',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/maltese-vs-maltipoo" schemas={schemas}>
  <section class="container-site pt-4">
    <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 px-6 py-10 md:px-12">
      <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} bare class="mb-5" />
      <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Comparison</p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] mb-3 max-w-[24ch]">Maltese vs Maltipoo: what does the Poodle change?</h1>
      <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-[52ch] mb-5">
        One is the parent, one is the cross, and our parent brand places both. Here is what
        actually changes when a Toy Poodle joins the family tree.
      </p>
      <a href={whatsappLink('Hi! Could you help me decide between a Maltese and a Maltipoo?')} class="btn-cta">Ask which fits you</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <AnswerCapsule question="Maltipoo or Maltese: what is the difference?">
    The difference between Maltese and Maltipoo comes down to coat and mind. A Maltese is the pure breed: straight silky white coat and classic lap-dog devotion. A Maltipoo, a Maltese Poodle mix, adds a Toy Poodle parent, which brings a curlier low-shedding coat in more
    colours (apricot, here), a quicker training mind, and the same wants-company nature. Both
    are HDB-listed; coat style and trainability are the practical deciders.
  </AnswerCapsule>

  <section class="container-site pt-8">
    <img
      src={featuredImg.src}
      width={featuredImg.width}
      height={featuredImg.height}
      alt="Maltipoo sitting beside a white Maltese among other small breeds"
      loading="lazy"
      class="rounded-[var(--radius-media)] w-full h-auto shadow-[var(--shadow-pop)]"
    />
  </section>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="The coat: silky curtain vs teddy curl" id="coat">
    <p>
      The maltese vs maltipoo decision (or maltipoo vs maltese, depending which face you saw first) usually gets made at the coat. The Maltese wears a
      straight, silky, always-white coat that mats into strings without near-daily brushing,
      or lives in a practical short cut. The Maltipoo wears the Poodle-influenced wave-to-curl
      that traps shed hair (good) and traps humidity tangles (the trade), in the apricot
      spectrum we mostly place.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tear stains are a shared reality; they simply show loudest on a white Maltese face. The
      daily eye-wipe routine from the <a href="/blog/maltipoo-tear-stains">tear-stain guide</a>
      applies to both.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Coat, side by side"
      items={[
        'Maltese: straight, silky, white, daily brushing',
        'Maltipoo: wavy-curly, low-shed, apricot here',
        'Both: tear stains, groom every 4 to 6 weeks',
        'Whose chore do you prefer: brushing or de-matting',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Temperament: same heart, quicker mind" id="temperament" reverse>
    <p>
      The heart is unchanged: the Maltese is the original velcro lap dog, and the maltipoo
      mixed with Maltese devotion keeps every bit of it, including the alert vocal streak and
      the need for daytime company covered in the
      <a href="/maltipoo-temperament">temperament guide</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The mind is where the Poodle shows. Toilet training and basic cues land faster with a
      Maltipoo, which is the single most practical difference for a first-time owner. Neither
      breed suits an empty weekday flat; that question outranks this whole page.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Temperament delta"
      items={[
        'Devotion: identical, both velcro',
        'Vocality: similar, both alert-barkers',
        'Training speed: Maltipoo noticeably faster',
        'Company needs: both high, no difference',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="HDB and the practical stuff" id="hdb" tinted>
    <p>
      No asymmetry here: the Maltese is named at item 33 of the
      <a href="https://www.hdb.gov.sg/managing-my-home/home-ownership/keeping-pets" rel="noopener" target="_blank">HDB approved list</a>,
      and the Maltipoo qualifies through item 62 as a cross of two approved breeds. Both
      finish toy-sized (see the <a href="/maltipoo-size">size guide</a>), ride carriers
      easily, and sit in the same grooming price tier.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Practical parity"
      items={[
        'HDB: Maltese item 33, Maltipoo via item 62',
        'Size: both toy class, 2 to 4kg territory',
        'Grooming tier: same, by weight',
        'Licence: same AVS rules and fees',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Who should pick which" id="verdict">
    <p>
      Pick the Maltese if the classic silky white look matters to you and near-daily brushing
      sounds like bonding rather than a chore. Pick the Maltipoo if you want the same devotion
      with an easier-training mind, a lower-shedding coat, and the apricot teddy look.
    </p>
    <p>
      We have no side to take: our parent brand Curious Tails places Maltese, and this shop
      places Maltipoos. Tell us your preference and routine on WhatsApp ({site.phoneDisplay})
      and you will get an honest answer either way.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="The one-line verdict"
      items={[
        'Classic white + brushing ritual: Maltese',
        'Faster training + teddy apricot: Maltipoo',
        'Empty weekday flat: honestly, neither',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />

  <CtaClose
    secondaryHeading="Compare more breeds"
    secondaryText="Cavapoo, Toy Poodle, Bichon, Shih Tzu and Cockapoo, all against the Maltipoo."
    secondaryHref="/compare-maltipoo"
    secondaryLabel="See all comparisons"
  />
</BaseLayout>
